  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Apps and host",
      "items": [
        "Web is apps/web (Next.js 16). Mobile is apps/mobile (Expo 54). Package manager is Bun.",
        "Vercel preview of integration is https://preview.tempoflow.dev (docs/ENVIRONMENTS.md). Production is https://www.tempoflow.dev (release.yml health check).",
        "Polar checkout route sets server to sandbox.",
        "Hostinger standalone bundle assembler exists (TEMPO-P42); it does not deploy or change DNS. Plan: hosting moves from Vercel to InsForge after the migration merges. Final host: UNKNOWN."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Backends: Convex to InsForge",
      "items": [
        "Backend is moving from Convex to InsForge (Amit, 2026-11-25; Firebase stopped). Plan: docs/backlog/INSFORGE-MIGRATION-PLAN.md. convex/ is read-only until Stage 5.",
        "InsForge: Postgres + RLS through @insforge/sdk, email OTP auth with an account gate, SQL in insforge/migrations/. Server ops folder apps/web/lib/server/ops/ is not on integration yet. Which InsForge project serves production: UNKNOWN.",
        "Convex (still live): dev tremendous-bass-443, staging ceaseless-dog-617 (test), prod precious-wildcat-890. convex-deploy-test pushes convex/ to the test deployment; prod deploys only from the Amit-only release flow."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "AI slots",
      "items": [
        "convex/lib/ai_router.ts calls https://api.deepinfra.com/v1/openai/chat/completions with native fetch (key: Convex env DEEPINFRA_API_KEY).",
        "Model is TEMPO_AI_MODEL, default deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash. Tiers fast, balanced and deep all map to it for now.",
        "MCP: external clients POST /mcp on Convex HTTP with a per-user token; apps/web/app/api/mcp proxies to it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust boundary",
      "items": [
        "People, Vercel, Polar, DeepInfra, MCP clients, and RevenueCat sit outside the Convex and InsForge security groups.",
        "Convex Auth, functions, and data sit in one group; InsForge Auth, API and Postgres in another (owner rows under RLS). The RevenueCat webhook and token-authenticated /mcp are the crossings into Convex.",
        "Web checkout calls Polar from the Next.js route. The access token stays in server env."
      ]
    }
  ]
